801	    /// `Cargo.toml` and differently-named `package.json` sharing one
802	    /// directory, per the test above) must resolve through
803	    /// `IdentityIndex.native`, keyed by the platform manifest's own npm
804	    /// name -- not the owning crate's `primary_id` name, which a
805	    /// sibling's dependency entry never names. Before this fix,
806	    /// `index.native` was keyed by `primary_id.name()` for every
807	    /// ecosystem in a Case D directory, so a dependency naming the
808	    /// platform package by its real npm name silently failed to resolve,
809	    /// dropping the edge with no diagnostic.
810	    #[test]
